welcome to the weird bacterial world of  zachary kopfer who wowed the internet  with this incredible microbial portrait  of einstein  so i'm zachary kopfer i'm a bio artist  who invented the method of  bacteriography which is basically a  process to grow photographs in bacteria  i love bacteria bacteria is gorgeous  there are all these different media that  make all these different colors with  different species and it's amazing the  variety you can get and i like the idea  that there's this invisible little  universe growing all over our skin and  with this work i'm taking that universe  and bring it into our perspective and  making it visible so we can see it  but how do you take a picture using  bacteria as film  zachary uses a nutrient-rich jelly or a  growth medium to create his artworks so  initially the bacteria are spread out  evenly across these plates we can't see  them of course because they're so small  but the colonies because they have a lot  of food here they're going to start to  grow then he takes a transparent sheet  with einstein's picture on it and he  shines ultraviolet light down  now the bacteria that are not shaded  from light are going to be hit by  ultraviolet rays which will damage their  dna and cause them to not be able to  reproduce but the bacteria that are  underneath the black parts are shielded  from ultraviolet light and they can  reproduce just fine  bacteria is essentially invisible to us  what better way to see it than in your  own portrait  i look at everything in life through the  perspective of science to me science is  beautiful sciences art science is poetry  and this work is a way for me to  translate my perspective into a visual  artifact for other people to actually  see  i wish i had my picture in bacteria but  he can do that we can get him to do that  now  we can help with that  i hope you like it adam
 

